# INTENTIONALLY EMPTY - no Source is registered by this module.
#
# PubSubSource used to be listed here, "pre-registered for sprint-4
# auto-config". It was removed in sprint-23 (Story 1.2) for two independent
# reasons:
#
#  1. NOT CONSTRUCTIBLE. Its constructors take (SubscriberStub,
#     subscriptionName) and (SubscriberStub, subscriptionName, maxMessages)
#     - PubSubSource.java:70 and PubSubSource.java:87 - so ServiceLoader
#     raised ServiceConfigurationError on every discovery pass. AutoConfig
#     swallowed that error before Story 1.1, so nothing ever said so.
#     Sprint 4 came and went; it is sprint 23.
#
#  2. Source IS NOT A ONE-PER-CLASSPATH CONTRACT. AutoConfig deliberately
#     exposes no singular source() accessor - only the plural sources()
#     (AutoConfig.java:264-266) - unlike warehouse(), blobStore() and
#     jobControl(). A pipeline reads from as many subscriptions as it has
#     input stages, and a subscription name is per-stage wiring, not
#     per-environment configuration. So there is no honest no-arg
#     constructor to write: a self-configuring PubSubSource would have to
#     pick ONE subscription out of the environment, and would be wrong for
#     every pipeline with two inputs.
#
# Removing the line is behaviour-identical to the swallowed error it
# replaces - discovery still yields no Source from this module - but it no
# longer advertises a lie, and it satisfies Story 1.2 AC 3.
#
# The class is unchanged and fully supported. Construct it per stage:
#     new PubSubSource(stub, ProjectSubscriptionName.of(p, s).toString())
